### Stock Portfolio Tracker - API Examples
### Base URL: http://localhost:8080/api

### ============================================
### USER MANAGEMENT
### ============================================

### Create a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "investor@example.com",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Investor",
  "password": "securePassword123"
}

### Get user by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### Get user by email
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/email/investor@example.com

### ============================================
### PORTFOLIO MANAGEMENT
### ============================================

### Create a new portfolio
POST http://localhost:8080/api/portfolios?userId=1&name=My%20Portfolio&description=My%20personal%20investment%20portfolio
Content-Type: application/json

### Get all portfolios for a user
GET http://localhost:8080/api/portfolios?userId=1

### Get specific portfolio
GET http://localhost:8080/api/portfolios/1?userId=1

### Refresh portfolio prices
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/portfolios/1/refresh-prices?userId=1

### ============================================
### TRANSACTIONS
### ============================================

### Create BUY transaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions?portfolioId=1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionType": "BUY",
  "ticker": "AAPL",
  "quantity": 10,
  "price": 150.25,
  "transactionDate": "2024-10-10T10:30:00",
  "notes": "Initial Apple purchase"
}

### Create another BUY transaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions?portfolioId=1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionType": "BUY",
  "ticker": "MSFT",
  "quantity": 5,
  "price": 380.50,
  "transactionDate": "2024-10-11T14:15:00",
  "notes": "Microsoft acquisition"
}

### Create SELL transaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions?portfolioId=1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionType": "SELL",
  "ticker": "AAPL",
  "quantity": 3,
  "price": 165.75,
  "transactionDate": "2024-10-12T09:45:00",
  "notes": "Partial profit taking"
}

### Create DIVIDEND transaction
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions?portfolioId=1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionType": "DIVIDEND",
  "ticker": "AAPL",
  "quantity": 0.5,
  "price": 0.23,
  "transactionDate": "2024-10-13T15:00:00",
  "notes": "Quarterly dividend"
}

### Get all transactions for a portfolio
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions?portfolioId=1

### Get transactions by date range
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/by-date-range?portfolioId=1&startDate=2024-10-01T00:00:00&endDate=2024-10-31T23:59:59

### ============================================
### ANALYTICS & REPORTING
### ============================================

### Generate portfolio analytics report
GET http://localhost:8080/api/analytics/report/1

### Response includes:
# - Total portfolio value and cost
# - Unrealized P&L
# - Return percentage
# - Asset allocation
# - Top and worst performers
# - Average cost per asset

### Get portfolio history (last 30 days)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/analytics/history/1?days=30

### Get portfolio history (last 90 days)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/analytics/history/1?days=90

### Get portfolio history (last year)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/analytics/history/1?days=365

### ============================================
### AI MARKET BRIEFING AGENT
### ============================================

### Generate market briefing with risk analysis
GET http://localhost:8080/api/briefings/1

### Response includes:
# - Portfolio overview summary
# - Risk assessment (LOW/MODERATE/HIGH)
# - Key identified risks
# - Actionable recommendations
# - Performance highlights

### ============================================
### WORKFLOW EXAMPLES
### ============================================

### Example 1: Complete Portfolio Setup
### Step 1: Create user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "trader@example.com",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Trader",
  "password": "tradePassword456"
}

# Assume userId = 2 from response

### Step 2: Create portfolio for user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/portfolios?userId=2&name=Tech%20Growth&description=Technology%20focused%20portfolio

# Assume portfolioId = 2 from response

### Step 3: Add multiple transactions
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions?portfolioId=2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionType": "BUY",
  "ticker": "TSLA",
  "quantity": 20,
  "price": 245.30,
  "transactionDate": "2024-09-01T10:00:00"
}

POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions?portfolioId=2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionType": "BUY",
  "ticker": "NVDA",
  "quantity": 15,
  "price": 875.50,
  "transactionDate": "2024-09-05T11:30:00"
}

### Step 4: Get portfolio details
GET http://localhost:8080/api/portfolios/2?userId=2

### Step 5: Refresh prices (get current valuations)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/portfolios/2/refresh-prices?userId=2

### Step 6: Generate analytics report
GET http://localhost:8080/api/analytics/report/2

### Step 7: Get market briefing
GET http://localhost:8080/api/briefings/2

### ============================================
### ERROR HANDLING EXAMPLES
### ============================================

### Invalid email format (will return 400 error)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Missing required field (will return 400 error)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Non-existent user (will return 400 error)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/9999

### Non-existent portfolio (will return 400 error)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/portfolios/9999?userId=1

### Insufficient quantity for sell (will return 400 error)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions?portfolioId=1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionType": "SELL",
  "ticker": "AAPL",
  "quantity": 1000,
  "price": 150.00,
  "transactionDate": "2024-10-15T10:00:00",
  "notes": "Trying to sell more than we own"
}
